This is an independent implementation of a network protocol, produced by
analysing how an existing client program communicates, for the purpose of
interoperability. It contains no code, artwork, audio or text taken from
KONAMI's software. It does contain tables of integers read mechanically
out of the client's data files, because a server cannot arbitrate this
protocol without them: branch targets, answer keys, the values a club
match is fought by, and the keys and gates a drama event is entered
through. They carry no question, no answer text, no line of dialogue, no
title, no character name, and no other text or imagery, and none is of
any use without a lawfully obtained copy of the game. Message names, map
names and structure offsets appear here because they are the identifiers
the protocol itself uses.

